@startuml
' Phase 7 — Toolbox: as-built infrastructure. Copied from plan.uml and edited
' to the finished state at phase end.

title Phase 7 — Toolbox (as built)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-toolbox (Go; imports contracts)" as toolbox {
  component "toolbox (types + errors + clock + idempotency)" as core
  component "registry (validated manifests + Provider seam)" as registry
  component "policy (capability intersection + sandbox + audit log)" as policy
  component "host (invocation + idempotent replay)" as host
  component "host.fake (deterministic provider)" as fake
  component "workflow (compiler: validate + deterministic topo plan)" as compile
  component "workflow (runtime: resume + retries + gates)" as runtime
  component "rpc (toolbox.invoke / compileWorkflow / registry)" as rpc
}

package "aa-contracts (tool_manifest + workflow + rpc-v1)" as contracts
package "aa-kernel (hosts the adapter, later)" as kernel
package "live MCP transport / OS sandbox enforcer (deferred)" as live

contracts --> registry
core --> registry
registry --> policy
policy --> host
registry --> host
fake --> host
core --> compile
compile --> runtime
host --> rpc
compile --> rpc
runtime --> rpc
live ..> host : mcp provider (deferred)
live ..> policy : os sandbox enforcer (deferred)
kernel ..> rpc : hosts over local socket

note right of registry
  ADR-P7-001/002: manifests are
  validated at registration; all
  kinds sit behind one Provider seam,
  so a new tool/MCP needed no core
  change in this phase.
end note

note bottom of policy
  ADR-P7-003/004/005: grant is the
  declared/contract intersection
  minus denials; every decision is
  audited; sandbox and network fail
  closed when required.
end note

note bottom of compile
  ADR-P7-006: cycles, self, duplicate,
  and dangling dependencies are
  rejected; order is deterministic and
  input-order independent.
end note

note bottom of runtime
  ADR-P7-007/008: resume from a deep-
  cloned serialized state; honor
  fail/retry/skip/compensate with
  bounded retries; nil gates await
  approval rather than proceed.
end note

note bottom of host
  ADR-P7-009: invocation is idempotent
  by a tool-namespaced key; replay
  returns the original result and never
  re-runs the provider.
end note

@enduml
